\section{Identification for Canvas}

The frontmatter carries only what [[canvaslms]] needs to find the
assignment: its name and a regular expression that matches the name
as it appears in the course.
The regular expression is the stable identifier; the name can be
edited in Canvas without breaking the match, as it was when the
assignment became a FeedbackFruits one.
Should the name ever stop containing the pattern, the assignment's
numeric Canvas id works in its place, since the pattern is matched
against both.
Due dates, module placement and publication state are left to the
Canvas interface, for the reason the onboarding page gives: those
fields belong to the course instance, not to the text, and a file
that carried a date would overwrite whatever the teacher set in the
course the next time it was published.

