\section{When something goes wrong}

The troubleshooting list covers the failures the venv-first route is
known to have, each stated as the symptom the student will see and
the check that resolves it.
Three of the four are the same failure seen from different places:
the terminal, the editor or the program using a Python other than the
course folder's.
The list therefore points back to the same two checks each time, the
[[(.venv)]] prefix and [[learnlog doctor]], rather than introducing
new commands to remember.
The Debian entry is the one platform-specific gap of the route: the
[[venv]] module ships in a separate package there.
The last entry protects a student who already uses Git from
committing the record into their own repository; [[.learnlog/]]
manages itself.

<<lab0: troubleshooting>>=
## Om något strular

- **Terminalen säger att `learnlog` inte finns:** terminalen använder
  inte kursmappens miljö. Kontrollera att prompten börjar med
  `(.venv)`; annars gör du om steg 2 och 3 under "Installera learnlog".
- **`learnlog list` visar inte din körning:** programmet kördes med en
  annan Python än kursmappens. Kör `learnlog doctor` i terminalen och
  kontrollera att VSCodium har valt tolken under `.venv` (**Python:
  Select Interpreter**).
- **`python3 -m venv .venv` misslyckas på Linux:** på Debian och Ubuntu
  behöver du först `sudo apt install python3-venv`.
- **Du använder redan Git i kursmappen:** mappen `.learnlog/` sköter
  sig själv. Lägg aldrig till den i ditt eget Git-förråd.

